<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Quintus Caecilius Metellus Numidicus</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">d. c. 91 BCE</span> · <a href="/centuries/2nd-century-bce">2nd century BCE</a> · Also known as Metellus Numidicus</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Quintus Caecilius Metellus Numidicus was a Roman general and leading conservative politician. As consul in 109 BCE he took command against <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/jugurtha">Jugurtha</a>, restored discipline and defeated him at the Muthul, but he was replaced by his former officer <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gaius-marius">Gaius Marius</a> in 107 BCE. He received a triumph and the name Numidicus, and was later exiled in 100 BCE for refusing to swear to a law of Saturninus.</p></div>
